IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgh-registers`
IMPORT `sgm-part5-div4`
IMPORT `sgm-part5-div4a`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- the procedure for getting at the register of members, as a regulative layer over the Boolean encodings in sgh-registers.l4 (s 12(2)(d)),
-- sgm-part5-div4.l4 (s 192(3) and (4)) and sgm-part5-div4a.l4 (s 196A).
--
-- What is here: s 12(2)(d), a person's access to the electronic register of members of a private company that the Registrar keeps under s 196A;
-- s 192(3) and (4), the request to a public company for a copy of its register and the company's 21 days to send it;
-- s 196A(1) and (5), the Registrar's two duties to keep and to update the electronic register.
-- The parties are the corpus's own `Party` (sg-core.l4). The gates are the existing section functions, called and not restated.
-- Each DEONTIC is gated: where the gate does not answer JUST TRUE, nothing is owed and the rule is FULFILLED at once (the text does not say what then happens).
-- Where the text puts no time limit on a step that is a thing to be done once (s 196A(5)), the step takes the found period that the section module takes for the same duty (notes/lest-without-deadline.md); a duty to keep a register (s 196A(1)) holds throughout and takes no clock.
-- Convention for the procedure units (assumed, not ruled): BREACH is kept only for a duty or a prohibition that the text lays on a named party; here that is the company's duty to send the copy and the Registrar's duty to update.

DECLARE `register access act` IS ONE OF
    `s 12(2)(d) obtain a copy of or an extract from the electronic register of members of the private company`
    `s 192(3) ask the public company for a copy of the register of members`
    `s 192(3) send the person the copy of the register that was asked for`
    `s 196A(1) the Registrar keeps and maintains the electronic register of members of the private company`
    `s 196A(5) the Registrar updates the electronic register of members for the change lodged`

§ `Section 12(2)(d): access to the electronic register of members of a private company`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the person, having paid the prescribed fee, obtains the copy or extract; counting=silent (the text puts no time limit on the person or on the Registrar)
-- The text gives the person a liberty ("may ... have access"). It names no duty of the Registrar to hand the copy over and no time for it: nothing is encoded for the Registrar (what the text leaves silent).
-- FORK: s 12(2)(d) | the Registrar has no step, because the text gives the person a liberty and names no duty or time for the Registrar | the Registrar MUST supply the copy, with no deadline
-- The permission stays open (a MAY with no limit): a person who never asks leaves it open, which the traces show as RESIDUAL.
-- src:2809 | (2) Any person may, on payment of the prescribed fee —
-- src:2828 | (d) have access to the electronic register of members of a
-- src:2829 | private company kept by the Registrar under section 196A
-- src:2830 | by obtaining a copy of or an extract from it.
@ref s 12(2)(d) access to the electronic register of members of a private company (src:2809-2830)
GIVEN person IS A Party
      `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register is the electronic register of members of a private company kept by the Registrar under section 196A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is one that the Minister has specified under subsection (2A), and the notification has not been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification under subsection (2A) was cancelled, and the document or certificate was filed, lodged or issued before the date of the cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `register access act`
`s 12(2)(d) the person may obtain a copy of or an extract from the electronic register of members once the prescribed fee is paid` MEANS
    IF `s 12(2)(d) the person may have access to the electronic register of members by obtaining a copy of or an extract from it` `the prescribed fee has been paid` `the register is the electronic register of members of a private company kept by the Registrar under section 196A` `the company is one that the Minister has specified under subsection (2A), and the notification has not been cancelled` `the notification under subsection (2A) was cancelled, and the document or certificate was filed, lodged or issued before the date of the cancellation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY person
         MAY `s 12(2)(d) obtain a copy of or an extract from the electronic register of members of the private company`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 192(3) and (4): the copy of a public company's register`

-- The number of days from the day the company receives the request to the last day for sending the copy (for the traces of the duty below).
-- The 21 days run from the day next after the day of receipt, so the last day is 21 days after receipt, and more by whatever further period the Registrar allows.
GIVEN `the day on which the request is received by the company` IS A DATE
      `the number of further days the Registrar considers reasonable in the circumstances, 0 if none` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 192(3) the number of days from the receipt of the request to the last day for sending the copy` MEANS
    (`s 192(3) the last day for sending the copy` `the day on which the request is received by the company` `the number of further days the Registrar considers reasonable in the circumstances, 0 if none`) MINUS `the day on which the request is received by the company`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day on which the public company receives the request (the day of the person's request is taken to be that day); counting="commencing on the day next after the day on which the request is received by the company", so the 21st day is day 21, and "within such further period as the Registrar considers reasonable in the circumstances" is added to the 21; the number of days is computed from the DATE inputs by `s 192(3) the number of days from the receipt of the request to the last day for sending the copy`
-- FORK: s 192(3) | the person's request and the company's receipt of it fall on the same day, which is day 0 | the company may receive the request on a later day than the person sends it, and the 21 days then run from that later day
-- FORK: s 192(3) | "such further period as the Registrar considers reasonable" is days added to the 21 | the further period replaces the 21 days as the whole period
-- FORK: s 192(4) | the offence is encoded as the consequence of the company's breach, in the BECAUSE of the LEST, because guilt is a status that nobody does; the officers in default are named in the BECAUSE and no officer is a party to the rule | each officer in default as a party of its own, with "in default" left as an input
-- (4) says nothing of a prosecution, a court act or a time for one: no court step is encoded after the breach.
-- The gate also asks that the sum was paid: the request is granted "on payment in advance" (src:17251-17252), so the company's duty to send arises on payment and not on the sum being merely one the subsection allows.
-- FORK: s 192(3) | the company's duty to send arises only once the sum required in advance, being one the subsection allows, has been paid | the duty arises when the request is made, whether or not the sum was paid
-- src:17248 | (3) Any member or other person may request the public company to
-- src:17249 | furnish that member or other person with a copy of the register, or of
-- src:17250 | any part thereof, but only so far as it relates to names, addresses,
-- src:17251 | number of shares held and amounts paid on shares, on payment in
-- src:17252 | advance of $1 or such less sum as the company requires for every
-- src:17253 | page thereof required to be copied and the company must cause any
-- src:17254 | copy so requested by any person to be sent to that person within a
-- src:17255 | period of 21 days or within such further period as the Registrar
-- src:17256 | considers reasonable in the circumstances commencing on the day
-- src:17257 | next after the day on which the request is received by the company.
@ref s 192(3) the copy of the register (src:17248-17257)
-- src:17261 | (4) If any copy so requested is not sent within the period prescribed
-- src:17262 | by subsection (3), the public company and every officer of the
-- src:17263 | company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:17264 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $400 and also to a default
-- src:17265 | penalty.
@ref s 192(4) the offence (src:17261-17265)
GIVEN person IS A Party
      `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the part of the register requested relates only to names, addresses, number of shares held and amounts paid on shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum the company requires in advance for every page, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum so required was paid in advance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the request is received by the company` IS A DATE
      `the number of further days the Registrar considers reasonable in the circumstances, 0 if none` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `register access act`
`s 192(3) the person may ask the public company for a copy of the register and the company must send it within the period` MEANS
    IF    `s 192(3) the person may request a copy of the part of the register` `the part of the register requested relates only to names, addresses, number of shares held and amounts paid on shares` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `s 192(3) the sum required in advance for a page is one the subsection allows` `the sum the company requires in advance for every page, in dollars` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `the sum so required was paid in advance`
    THEN PARTY person
         MAY `s 192(3) ask the public company for a copy of the register of members`
         HENCE (PARTY Company `the name of the company`
                MUST `s 192(3) send the person the copy of the register that was asked for`
                WITHIN (`s 192(3) the number of days from the receipt of the request to the last day for sending the copy` `the day on which the request is received by the company` `the number of further days the Registrar considers reasonable in the circumstances, 0 if none`)
                HENCE FULFILLED
                LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the copy of the register was not sent within the 21 days, or the further period the Registrar considers reasonable, so the public company and every officer of the company in default are guilty of an offence under section 192(4)")
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 196A(1) and (5): the Registrar keeps and updates the electronic register`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the Registrar's duty is asked about (the duty runs "On and after 3 January 2016", which the gate checks); counting=silent (the text states no period within which the register is to be kept)
-- The duty is a standing one with no limit: the traces show it as RESIDUAL until the Registrar does the act, and no breach is possible.
-- FORK: s 196A(1) | a duty to keep and maintain a register holds throughout (class MAINTENANCE in notes/lest-without-deadline.md) and carries no LEST and no BREACH, because no period can run out on it | a MUST with a LEST BREACH that can never be reached
-- So the rule carries no LEST and no BREACH, as the section module `sgm-part5-div4a.l4` carries none for this duty (the comment beside its rule, "no LEST: no deadline is modelled for this duty ... [class: maintenance]").
-- src:17447 | 196A.—(1) On and after 3 January 2016, the Registrar must, in
-- src:17448 | respect of every private company, keep and maintain an electronic
-- src:17449 | register of members of that company containing such information
-- src:17450 | notified to the Registrar on or after that date.
@ref s 196A(1) the Registrar must keep the electronic register (src:17447-17450)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `register access act`
`s 196A(1) the Registrar must keep and maintain an electronic register of members, as a standing duty` MEANS
    IF `s 196A(1) the Registrar must keep an electronic register of members of the company` `the company is a private company` `the date asked` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Registrar
         MUST `s 196A(1) the Registrar keeps and maintains the electronic register of members of the private company`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the change that is required or authorised to be lodged is lodged with the Registrar; counting=silent in the text, so the period is the input `the period of all convenient speed, as found` (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"; found by whoever applies the rule; no default)
-- The duty is one to do a thing once on a trigger the text names (the lodging), class ACHIEVEMENT, s 52 (notes/lest-without-deadline.md); the layer gives it the same input as `sgm-part5-div4a.l4` gives the same duty, so the two layers answer one question alike (decided by Claude on 2026-11-27, assumed, not ruled).
-- FORK: s 196A(5) | the update is owed within the period of all convenient speed, found as an input, and an update after it is a BREACH of the Registrar | the update has no clock and the duty stays open for ever, which is the layer's first reading
-- src:17512 | (5) The Registrar must update the electronic register of members in
-- src:17513 | accordance with any change that is required or authorised by any
-- src:17514 | provision of this Act to be lodged with the Registrar, including
-- src:17515 | section 31(1), 63(1), 70(6), 71(1B), 74A(3), 76B(7), 76K(1A), 126(2)
-- src:17516 | or 128(1)(a).
@ref s 196A(5) the Registrar must update the electronic register (src:17512-17516)
GIVEN `the change is lodged under section 31(1), 63(1), 70(6), 71(1B), 74A(3), 76B(7), 76K(1A), 126(2) or 128(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is required or authorised by another provision of this Act to be lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `register access act`
`s 196A(5) the Registrar must update the electronic register of members for a change lodged` MEANS
    IF `s 196A(5) the Registrar must update the electronic register of members in accordance with the change` `the change is lodged under section 31(1), 63(1), 70(6), 71(1B), 74A(3), 76B(7), 76K(1A), 126(2) or 128(1)(a)` `the change is required or authorised by another provision of this Act to be lodged with the Registrar` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Registrar
         MUST `s 196A(5) the Registrar updates the electronic register of members for the change lodged`
         WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not update the electronic register of members in accordance with the change lodged within the period of all convenient speed"
    ELSE FULFILLED
